# REST Client / PhpStorm: set apiKey to a generated plaintext key.
# Generate with: docker compose exec php bin/console apikey:generate mobile
# Store the mobile:hash output in .env API_KEY_HASHES and recreate PHP/Nginx.
# Send X-Api-Key with hyphens; X_API_KEY is not accepted by Nginx.
# Defaults match .env.example; change baseUrl if APP_PORT differs.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082
@apiKey = REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_GENERATED_KEY
@email = requests-client@example.com
@password = REPLACE_WITH_A_RANDOM_PASSWORD
@userId = 1

### Public database health: 200, or 503 when DB is unavailable
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Nginx-only health: 200; does not check MySQL
GET {{baseUrl}}/nginx-health

### Unknown route: 404 JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/nope

### Wrong method: 405 and Allow: GET
POST {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Protected route without a key: 401 and WWW-Authenticate: ApiKey
GET {{baseUrl}}/users

### List users: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?limit=20&offset=0
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-Request-Id: requests-list-001

### Limit above 100: 422 with details.limit
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?limit=200&offset=1
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Show an existing user: set userId after creation or use a seeded ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/show?id={{userId}}
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Invalid ID: 422 with details.id
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/show?id=abc
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Missing user: normally 404 on the demo database
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/show?id=999999999
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Create: 201, Location and data; repeat the same email for 409 email_taken
# Use a new email for another successful creation.
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{email}}","password":"{{password}}"}

### Validation: 422 with email and password details
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"invalid","password":""}

### Wrong media type: 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: text/plain

{}

### Invalid JSON: 400 before route middleware
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":

### Nginx CORS preflight: 204, without an API key
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/users
Origin: https://client.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Content-Type, X-Api-Key
